    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d199">

                <pb facs="0197" n="187" sameAs="frus:frus1949v09/pg187"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.01/11–949: Airgram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in the United Kingdom</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Bliss</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">London</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1949-11-09">November 9,
                        1949</date>.<lb/>[Received November 14—1:22 p. m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>A–2062. [Here follows report on Singapore Conference similar in substance to
                    report given in memorandum of conversation on November 8, printed on <ref
                        target="#pg184">page 184</ref>.]</p>
                <p>On the afternoon of November 8, Mr. Peter Scarlett, Head of Far Eastern
                    Department, Foreign Office … stated that, although in general the reactions
                    received from the interested friendly governments up to the present were only of
                    a preliminary nature (Embtel 4353, October 31<anchor n="17" xml:id="d199-f1"/>),
                    on the whole they were sympathetic with the British inclination toward early
                    recognition. Two of the powers consulted had emphasized that it would be
                    embarrassing to recognize the new government before the end of the present
                    session of the UNGA.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Bliss</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
